            <div xml:id="d138">

                <pb facs="0282" n="170" sameAs="frus:frus1919Russia/pg170"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">123 T 71/124: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Commission to Negotiate Peace to the Acting
                        Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-02-08T16:00:00+00:00"><hi rendition="#italic">February 8,
                                1919, 4 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received February 9, 3:34
                        p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>660. Department’s 457, January 28, 6 p.m. and 563, February 4, 5 p.m.<anchor
                        n="39" xml:id="d138-f1"/> Detention of Tredwell and Kalamatiano has received
                    careful consideration by Commission. The Prinkipo proposal has been made to
                    various factions in Russia and could not be consequent upon [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">considered</hi>] a communication to Soviet Government
                    alone. I believe American delegates should be advised to make informal
                    representations. If any further method of bringing influence to bear is
                    discovered all possible steps will be taken. I assume that you will further
                    investigate possibility of exchange against three hostages held by Government of
                    India. Their reluctance to return to Bolshevist territory seems irrelevant.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi></signed>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Am</hi>[<hi rendition="#small-caps">erican</hi>] <hi
                        rendition="#small-caps">Mission</hi></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
